# Phone-first UI

Design and implement pages for a phone viewport first (~390px wide). Desktop/tablet is progressive enhancement, not the default canvas.

## Layout

- Single column by default. Avoid multi-column grids until `md:` or later.
- Prefer stacked lists/cards over wide tables on small screens (tables only from `md:` up if needed).
- Keep primary actions thumb-reachable (bottom nav / sticky bottom CTA is fine; don’t bury actions in a top-only desktop chrome).
- Respect safe areas: `pb-[max(...,env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]` on fixed bottom UI.
- Cap content width for readability; don’t force desktop dashboard density on phones.

## Interaction & type

- Touch targets ≥ ~44px (`btn-md` / comfortable padding). No hover-only affordances for critical actions.
- Body text stays readable at 16px+; don’t shrink UI to fit more widgets.
- One clear job per screen section; reduce competing CTAs above the fold.

## Implementation habits

- Write base Tailwind classes for mobile; add `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` only when needed.
- Reuse tokens in `components/styles.ts` and the existing `DashboardShell` bottom-nav pattern.
- When adding a new page, verify the first viewport on a phone width before polishing desktop.

## Out of scope

API routes, migrations, and server-only `lib/` code are unaffected by this rule.
